    "show_share": true,
    "description": "For many Kenyan families, dementia is a silent struggle; misunderstood, often ignored and wrapped in stigma. When a loved one starts forgetting names, getting lost in familiar places, or struggling to communicate, it is commonly dismissed as \"just old age.\" In some cases, cultural beliefs blame supernatural forces, delaying much-needed medical help. By the time families seek care, the disease has often progressed to an advanced stage.",
